\item \strong{Verified follow-up}: an outcome event, or evidence (see \code{followup_evidence}) dated \verb{>= anchor + F},
where the anchor is \code{e} (\code{s} for fixed-window mortality).
\item \strong{Leak-free scoping}: history lies at or before \code{s} and outcomes strictly after the anchor, so lookback
and outcome periods are disjoint. \code{study_window} restricts only the index date; follow-up and outcome
ascertainment may use records after \code{study_end}.
}
